## Warm Start Optimization v2 (2026-09-02)

Branch `perf/warm-start-optimization` on both `bansaldeepak/Realtime-Avatar` and `Panya-Labs/MuseTalk`.
PR: https://github.com/Panya-Labs/MuseTalk/pull/38

### Results (validated with live Docker restarts + WebRTC sessions)

- **Warm start (Docker restart):** 69s → 14.3s (4.8x). TF removal pending rebuild → ~12.5s est.
- **Per-session greeting:** 1610ms → 774ms (2.1x). Render service thread eliminates cuDNN per-thread autotuning.

### Key technical findings

- cuDNN benchmark plans are **per-thread** (verified: ~450ms/shape autotuning even after warming on another thread)
- UNet safetensors .pth→.safetensors conversion done inside container at `/app/models/musetalkV15/unet.safetensors`
- base_part_inter cached as uint8 .npy (279MB), max pixel error ±0.5 (invisible)
- TF removal from requirements.txt committed but needs Docker image rebuild to take effect
- `bansaldeepak/Realtime-Avatar` has upstream remote `Panya-Labs/MuseTalk` configured

### Commits (5 on the branch)

1. `0ab0bab` — Lazy model loading + safetensors UNet + batch VAE
2. `82d3e87` — Cache blend_params, reduce warmup, page cache pre-warming, remove TF
3. `b8635ce` — A/B test documentation
